<title>DUBAI: Saudi Aramco revises bunker fuel prices.</title>
<headline>Saudi Aramco revises bunker fuel prices.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saudi Aramco has increased A-960 bunker fuel prices from Ras Tanura and Dammam by $2 a tonne to $104 a tonne ($15.96 a barrel) with effect June 19, it said.</p>
<p>A-960 from the Red Sea ports of Jeddah and Yanbu was raised 50 cents to $99 a tonne ($15.20).</p>
<p>A-888 bunker diesel from Ras Tanura and Dammam was cut $2 to $204 a tonne and $1 higher at $180 a tonne from Red Sea ports.</p>
</text>
